  "body": "The PR test job now runs on any self-hosted runner carrying `camcraft-pr-test` (Linux `uma`, macOS `m3`): `runs-on` drops the `linux` label. The workflow steps were already bash 3.2 / BSD-tool safe, so nothing else in them changed. Header comments, AGENTS.md \"The PR test runner\", PR-reviewer.md (runner-online check now keys on `camcraft-pr-test`) and review-prs/SKILL.md are updated to match.\n\nMaintainer, 2026-11-14: \"so change it.. so we can run on both - push the change without an issue and just get it merged right away should be a oneline fix.\"\n\nNot exercised: no run on the macOS runner yet; macOS arms of per-OS pinned tests unchecked; UI suites on macOS need a logged-in session.\n\nChangelog: none\nProcess change: yes\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
